Z||000002||Standard||03-30-2001||12:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> The guy I know doing the 3400 swap has an 86 SE black on black factory.Yes I am 100% sure, his dad was the one who ordered the car new in '85.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's still not a true monochrome car, the ground f/x are a matte black, while the rest is glossy black.  Two different paint codes.  You could also get a silver GT/SE with silver ground f/x, but they're different paint codes, too.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||03-30-2001||07:51 AM||||Right on, Standard. I'll try to dig up the FOCOA article, it said the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||03-30-2001||10:33 AM||||I remember the article about those cars, too.  Only 20 or 30 of them were sold, the rest were returned to the factory and converted back to normal GT's.  All of those cars also had big pegasus decals (supplied by FOCOA) installed on the hood at the plant, so I don't think this is one of them.  Don't know why'd you'd repaint a car with 30,000 miles on it, though... hmmmm..||||reg||1
